<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Surrender of Japan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2 September <a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · <a href="/today-in-history/september-2">On this day: 2 September</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The surrender of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> was formally signed on 2 September 1945 aboard the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uss-missouri">USS Missouri</a> in Tokyo Bay. It ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a> treat it as the end of the empire, followed by Allied occupation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/surrender-of-japan.jpg" alt="Surrender of Japan" width="320" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Army Signal Corps photographer LT. Stephen E. Korpanty; restored by Adam Cuerden · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mamoru_Shigemitsu_signs_the_Instrument_of_Surrender,_officially_ending_the_Second_World_War.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
